      children: ["Most “surprising” outages aren't surprises. They're the moment the bill comes due for decisions that felt rational at the time: a rushed launch, a deferred migration, a skipped dependency update, a fragile pipeline that “usually works.” Teams don't wake up and choose disaster. They slowly accept a set of tradeoffs that reduce their margin for error until the system has no slack left. The brutal part is that the organization usually ", _jsx(_components.em, {
